                ('How is the Finger Saw cleaned after use?', 'After use, the Finger Saw should be rinsed immediately to prevent bone debris from drying on the blade serrations. It should then be ultrasonically cleaned, rinsed thoroughly, dried, and autoclaved following standard veterinary surgical instrument sterilisation protocols. The blade should be inspected for dullness or damage before each use.'),
