                ('What tendons are harvested with the Tendon Stripper in veterinary surgery?', 'In veterinary orthopaedic surgery, the Tendon Stripper is most commonly used to harvest the long digital extensor tendon, semitendinosus, or gracilis tendons for use as autografts in cranial cruciate ligament reconstruction. The choice of donor tendon depends on the patient\'s size, the required graft dimensions, and the surgeon\'s preferred reconstruction technique.'),
                ('How is the Tendon Stripper sized for different patients?', 'Tendon Strippers are available in multiple head diameters to accommodate different tendon sizes across veterinary patient species and breeds. The correct size is selected based on the estimated diameter of the tendon being harvested, ensuring the cutting head engages the tendon without excessive compression or tearing during the stripping manoeuvre.'),
