                ('How do Tendon Tunnelling Forceps differ from standard haemostatic forceps?', 'Tendon Tunnelling Forceps have longer, more substantially curved shafts and blunter tips than standard haemostatic forceps, designed specifically for penetrating and navigating through tissue planes over longer distances. Their jaws are optimised for grasping and pulling bulkier materials such as tendon grafts and thick sutures rather than for vessel clamping.'),
